  "_doc": "Identifier-PART query suite (proposal B1, docs/audits/20260927-oss-landscape-optimization-proposal.md). Each query names a PART of a camelCase / PascalCase identifier that one seed-data.json row carries (useLayoutEffect, terminationGracePeriodSeconds, windowSoftInputMode, ...), either as spaced words ('layout effect') or as a Pascal fragment ('LayoutEffect'). relevant_ids = every seed row carrying that identifier (structural ground truth, not a judgement call). Selection rule: a query was admitted ONLY if it scored R@10 = 0 on the pre-B1 tree (2026-09-27, main @ 209a8bd, production_hybrid) AND the relevant row does not contain the query as a literal substring — so the suite measures identifier splitting and nothing else. Rejected at construction because they already hit on the pre-B1 tree: 'soft input mode', 'visible content position', 'IgnoreDifferences' (case-folds to the whole identifier), 'root margin' (in the prose), 'owner authentication biometrics', 'termination grace', 'busy buffers size' (snake_case — unicode61 already splits '_'). Run via benchmark/denoise-ab.mjs (suite identifier_parts).",
